# Root git attributes (CR-008 / ISS-178). Without this file, `pnpm
# --filter @rogikotha/test-support port` and `pnpm fixtures:build` always
# write LF, `core.autocrlf=true` checks the same files out CRLF on
# Windows, and every regeneration leaves `git status --porcelain` dirty
# with EOL-only changes even though the content is byte-identical.
#
# `infra/compose/.gitattributes` already forces LF for the files bind-
# mounted into Linux containers there (a more specific path wins over this
# file); this one is the repo-wide default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixture/derivative binaries: never let git's text auto-detection or EOL
# normalisation touch these, or a real binary payload gets corrupted the
# way `report.pdf` (T-007 / ISS-178) was.
*.pdf binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
# Web fonts (T-011, design F9): the self-hosted Hind Siliguri subset is a binary payload.
*.woff2 binary
